payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3d59bcbda6c21b1c64ec0de014f416cdf01d6e7168131efb25c844c8b34f1622","event_uuid":"20686457-03ea-4985-a9e9-1a2aa58fa8e9","position":{"commit_sha":"a2e39a60da9ca2259081d617793dcf85f7d80eae","position":"1787536349390998001-20686457-03ea-4985-a9e9-1a2aa58fa8e9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3fe657fb2d9420daf1ed7c0d64e235b1f6e189cf479294bfea748e003e2317ed","event_uuid":"bd7c4739-65d3-41c0-975a-fba6112db5e7","position":{"commit_sha":"9b17ecae0bc1d5103b883ca91891682af588105f","position":"1787536382014028001-bd7c4739-65d3-41c0-975a-fba6112db5e7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence is recorded in session log holohedral-deadbeat-tenrec. The implementation skill now requires atomic claim, omits an assignee by default, documents configured and empty default-assignee behavior, restricts explicit Jira overrides to email or accountId, and removes the direct start-work transition alternative. The brainstorm skill now distinguishes a completed current-cycle action from a successful review verdict and documents unsigned INDETERMINATE, coverage.llm_ran set to false, exit status 2, deferred evaluation, dependency order, and the agent force prohibition. The focused workflow suite passed six tests. The skill packaging suite passed twenty tests. The frontmatter gate, documentation index check, lint gate, and type check passed. The full suite was skipped under operator direction. Ticket arid-gutless-myna retained its closed status, description, and acceptance criteria while receiving one append-only correction comment. Gerrit change 2165 passed LLM-Review and Verified with no unresolved comments, then merged as e48142648445. No residual gaps or deferred review findings remain.","timestamp":1787535313801563001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787509275472300001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e42861bc-233a-4223-ac3f-11a38adf7f2d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"20f3-56b5-6e97-4de3"},{"link_uuid":"86028ecf-ac44-43b9-8c03-53f47777bee2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4e91-6008-97ca-4454"},{"link_uuid":"e22d94c2-38b4-4e56-bcb8-cdafcb872253","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a5ca-8d5a-279d-47f5"}],"description":"## Context\n\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md` teaches explicit bare assignees and offers direct status transition as an alternative to atomic claim. `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md` describes an unsigned claimability fast-fail as a successful review cycle. Tickets comely-craven-apatosaur and stealthful-calmy-erin establish the enforced claim and review behavior. Ticket arid-gutless-myna introduced the inaccurate successful-cycle wording and requires an append-only correction. Dependency helpful-stale-wildcat established the portable identity rule in `templates/rebar-usage.md` and `templates/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Create `tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py` before editing either skill. The tests assert atomic claim, conditional identity behavior, removal of the direct transition alternative, blocked-review deferral, unsigned `INDETERMINATE` semantics, dependency order, and the agent-force prohibition. Run the focused test and record RED before the documentation change.\n- Replace every start-work alternative in the implementation skill with atomic `rebar claim <id>`. Atomic claim prevents two agents from claiming the same ticket.\n- Remove direct `rebar transition <id> open in_progress` as a start-work alternative.\n- Apply the identity rule from `templates/rebar-usage.md` and `templates/AGENTS.md`. Run claim without `--assignee`. A configured `ticket.default_assignee` applies that identity. An empty setting leaves the claimed ticket unassigned. Pass `--assignee` only for an explicit override. An override in a Jira-reconciled store must use email or accountId. Never prescribe a bare handle.\n- State in the brainstorm skill that the current-cycle agent action is complete for blocked work, so the agent waits until the ticket becomes claimable.\n- State that the claimability fast-fail returns unsigned `INDETERMINATE` with `coverage.llm_ran` set to false and exit status 2. This result defers the LLM verdict. It is not a PASS, passing attestation, or successful review verdict.\n- Preserve dependency-order guidance and the prohibition on agent force.\n- Capture `rebar show arid-gutless-myna --output json` before adding a `rebar comment` that cites the enforced behavior. Read it again afterward and confirm that the status, description, and acceptance criteria are unchanged while the new comment is present. Do not edit or reopen the ticket.\n- Run the focused workflow test, skill packaging tests, frontmatter gate, and documentation index check.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The implementation skill requires atomic `rebar claim` for starting work.\n- [x] The implementation skill no longer offers `rebar transition <id> open in_progress` as a start-work alternative.\n- [x] The implementation skill presents claim without an explicit assignee as the default.\n- [x] The implementation skill describes configured and empty `ticket.default_assignee` behavior.\n- [x] Explicit override guidance requires email or accountId only for a Jira-reconciled store and never prescribes a bare handle.\n- [x] The brainstorm skill states that the current-cycle agent action is complete for blocked work until the ticket becomes claimable.\n- [x] The brainstorm skill states that unsigned `INDETERMINATE` is not a PASS, passing attestation, or successful verdict.\n- [x] Both skills retain dependency-order guidance.\n- [x] Both skills prohibit agent force.\n- [x] `rebar show arid-gutless-myna --output json` confirms one new correction comment while status, description, and acceptance criteria remain unchanged.\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py -q` passes.\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py -q` passes.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` passes.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","reason":"Correct atomic claim and identity guidance."},{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md","reason":"Correct blocked plan review and unsigned verdict guidance."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py","reason":"Pin the corrected workflow contracts in focused tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","20f3-56b5-6e97-4de3"],["parent","b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4"],["relates_to","4e91-6008-97ca-4454"],["relates_to","a5ca-8d5a-279d-47f5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","parent_status_